From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:17:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: cool on PMH0110
 F / G / I heat

The vendor binds cooling to the 95 C stage of three PMH0110 temperature
alarms:
- pmh0110_f_tz: the GPU from cooling state 5 (826 MHz) upwards;
- pmh0110_g_tz: pause CPUs 2-5;
- pmh0110_i_tz: pause CPUs 6-7.

The zones and their trips (95 C passive, 115 C hot, 145 C critical) come
from pmh0110-kaanapali.dtsi without maps. Add the maps. Mainline has no
CPU pause cooling device, so the cluster is held at its lowest frequency
instead, as in the XO zone (cpufreq state 27 = 384000 kHz, state 28 =
768000 kHz). The vendor's fourth map (PMH0110 D: CDSP and modem) has
nothing to bind to here.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts    | 32 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 64a38d2ff3c6..4b48032187c9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -2379,6 +2379,38 @@ usb-temp-r-hot {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * PMIC temperature alarms: stock binds cooling to the 95 C stage of three PMH0110 zones: F -> the GPU from 826 MHz
+ * down, G -> pause CPUs 2-5, I -> pause CPUs 6-7. Mainline has no CPU pause, so the cluster is held at its lowest
+ * frequency instead (as in the XO zone).
+ */
+&{/thermal-zones/pmh0110-f-thermal} {
+	cooling-maps {
+		map0 {
+			trip = <&{/thermal-zones/pmh0110-f-thermal/trips/trip0}>;
+			cooling-device = <&gpu 5 THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&{/thermal-zones/pmh0110-g-thermal} {
+	cooling-maps {
+		map0 {
+			trip = <&{/thermal-zones/pmh0110-g-thermal/trips/trip0}>;
+			cooling-device = <&cpu0 27 27>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&{/thermal-zones/pmh0110-i-thermal} {
+	cooling-maps {
+		map0 {
+			trip = <&{/thermal-zones/pmh0110-i-thermal/trips/trip0}>;
+			cooling-device = <&cpu6 28 28>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
 /* CPU thermal trips mirroring stock 11.A.38 */
 /*
  * kaanapali.dtsi only has hot (120 C) and critical (125 C) CPU trips. Stock throttles from 105 C (thermal
-- 
